            "description": "[confidence=high, sources=dynamic,static] The malware string 'FindFirstFile' was found in the binary, alongside 1 other string(s) also characteristic of File and Directory Discovery. Multiple corroborating strings, not this one in isolation, is what makes this a strong signal. | The malware string 'FindNextFile' was found in the binary, alongside 1 other string(s) also characteristic of File and Directory Discovery. Multiple corroborating strings, not this one in isolation, is what makes this a strong signal. | The API functions FindClose, FindFirstFileW, FindNextFileW are all imported by the binary. This combination is characteristic of File and Directory Discovery \u2014 multiple corroborating APIs together, not one import in isolation, is what makes this a strong signal. | CAPE signature 'folder_enumeration' fired (severity=3, confidence=70%, categories=['ransomware', 'wiper', 'infostealer', 'discovery'])",
