            "name": "Virtualization/Sandbox Evasion",
            "description": "[confidence=high, sources=static] The malware string 'Sleep' was found in the binary, alongside 2 other string(s) also characteristic of Virtualization/Sandbox Evasion. Multiple corroborating strings, not this one in isolation, is what makes this a strong signal. | The malware string 'GetSystemInfo' was found in the binary, alongside 2 other string(s) also characteristic of Virtualization/Sandbox Evasion. Multiple corroborating strings, not this one in isolation, is what makes this a strong signal. | The malware string 'QueryPerformanceCounter' was found in the binary, alongside 2 other string(s) also characteristic of Virtualization/Sandbox Evasion. Multiple corroborating strings, not this one in isolation, is what makes this a strong signal. | The API functions Sleep, GetSystemInfo, QueryPerformanceCounter, QueryPerformanceFrequency are all imported by the binary. This combination is characteristic of Virtualization/Sandbox Evasion \u2014 multiple corroborating APIs together, not one import in isolation, is what makes this a strong signal.",
            "external_references": [
                {
                    "source_name": "mitre-attack",
                    "url": "https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1497/",
