            "created": "2026-08-28T14:53:37.862228Z",
            "modified": "2026-08-28T14:53:37.862228Z",
            "name": "Disable or Modify Tools",
            "description": "[confidence=high, sources=dynamic,static] The API functions OpenProcess, TerminateProcess, WTSEnumerateProcessesW are all imported by the binary. This is a coherent enumerate-then-kill primitive: deliberately searching the process list (WTSEnumerateProcessesW) rather than acting on a handle already held, then opening and terminating a match. Consistent with Disable or Modify Tools (T1685) even without a decrypted target name to confirm which process is targeted -- medium rather than high confidence for that reason. | CAPE signature 'amsi_enumeration' fired (severity=3, confidence=40%, categories=['discovery', 'defense_evasion'])",
            "external_references": [
